  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q41-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "41",
    "prompt": "Find the value of $n$ such that the coefficient of $x^2$ is 385 in the expansion of\n$$(1+x)^n+(1+2x)^{2n}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=7$.",
      "worked": "The coefficient of $x^2$ is $\\binom{n}{2}+4\\binom{2n}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n}{2}+4\\binom{2n}{2}&=385\\\\\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}+4\\frac{2n(2n-1)}{2}&=385\\\\17n^2-9n-770&=0\\\\(n-7)(17n+110)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $n=7$ or $n=-\\frac{110}{17}$. Since $n$ is a non-negative integer, $n=7$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
